      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FANTAXTIC (6) turned things around last start and landed the prize by 3/4 of a length over 1200m at this track, which was the third run back from a spell. Peak fitness now, gets some weight relief via the claim and can win again. LUCKY I AM (4) has raced in similar company the past few starts and hasn't been beaten all that far. Gets the chance to be a key player again. SATURDAY SESH (1) resumes here and is generally better later in the campaign but has won first-up in the past and strikes the right grade of race to show up fresh. LET'S TALK (2) was out of the money two runs back then again missed the frame last start over 1100m at Northam, beaten 2.75 lengths into fifth but looks suited in this company. Improvement expected. RIPPER FAROOQ (3) booted up from the inside draw to race on the speed only to be claimed late and finish 3 lengths away in fifth last start over 1200m at this track. Among the chances.",
